# Topic ACLs (NFR-SEC-02). Anything not granted here is refused: a publish is
# dropped with "not authorised", a subscription is refused, a message is not
# delivered.
#
# ADR-0003: so-gateway is the only service on thing/ and sys/. Every other
# service is confined to so/internal/. The one outside client is the Cloud API
# client (FR-DEV-06), which reads the dock's side and writes only the topics a
# cloud platform sends on.
#
# tools/tests/test_infra.py holds this file to those rules, and
# infra/tests/test_stack.py attempts every forbidden publish against the broker.

user so-gateway
topic readwrite thing/#
topic readwrite sys/#
topic readwrite so/internal/#
# The broker's log, where FR-DEV-06's takeover shows up: Mosquitto logs
# "Client cloud-client already connected, closing old connection." at error
# level, and who took over at notice level ("New client connected from
# <address> as cloud-client"). infra/tests/test_stack.py holds both levels.
topic read $SYS/broker/log/E
topic read $SYS/broker/log/N

user so-fleet
topic readwrite so/internal/#

user so-wayline
topic readwrite so/internal/#

user so-bridge
topic readwrite so/internal/#

# DJI Cloud API topic directions, cloud to dock. The client reads everything the
# dock publishes and writes nothing the dock would.
user cloud-client
topic read thing/#
topic read sys/#
topic write thing/product/+/services
topic write thing/product/+/property/set
topic write thing/product/+/events_reply
topic write thing/product/+/requests_reply
topic write thing/product/+/drc/down
topic write sys/product/+/status_reply

# The container's own health check. Its password is random per start and never
# leaves the container.
user broker-healthcheck
topic read $SYS/broker/uptime
